        "result": "Captured, with nothing accepted. Graph revision moved from 3 to 4 with 13 changes, applied through `./tg apply` with the batch shown above.\n\n**Candidate failure mode, as extracted**\n\nIndividually useful reviews can keep generating further reviews with no effective stop and no ruling on what comes next, so the intention ends up served manually outside Morphisms. The summary shows two separate gaps: nobody ended the attempt, and nobody ruled on subsequent work. It does not say who should have done either, so no role is assigned.\n\n**What a stop threshold and steward handoff might address**\n\n- A stop threshold could bound how long reviews may spawn reviews before the attempt ends. The accepted threshold-ending claim already allows ending unproductive work at a configured threshold, but M1688's reviews were each useful, so it is untested whether any threshold would have tripped.\n- A steward handoff at ending could supply the missing ruling, since the steward already owns choosing subsequent work under the current decision.\n- Neither mechanism, on its own, says what happens to the concern after the attempt stops. That is the gap your question points at.\n\n**What was written**\n\n- `m1688-summary-source`, a synthetic verbatim source, graded as a secondary summary with the primary postmortem marked unavailable.\n- `m1688-review-loop-failure-mode`, a claim with status proposed and review state needs-review, anchored to end-attempt and choose-work.\n- `m1688-stop-and-handoff-proposal`, a claim with status proposed, marked threshold unchosen and stopping authority unsettled. It depends on the failure mode and does not revise threshold-ending or the steward decision.\n- `m1688-concern-persistence-question`, open, answer shape condition, anchored to end-attempt and the CPU intention as the example of a concern that must outlive an attempt.\n\nThe consultation question stays open and untouched. `./tg check` reports no structural errors and no new tensions.\n\n**The question for you:** when a review-generating attempt is terminated, what rule keeps the underlying concern alive afterward? For example, does the intention stay open on the steward's queue, does the terminating party have to record an explicit carry-forward, or is there a different mechanism? No candidate answer is recorded.",
